## TL;DR: Emerald Cut Diamond Size at a Glance

Emerald cut diamond size comparison shows one consistent pattern: this shape runs long and narrow. The length reads larger than a round brilliant of the same carat weight; the width is smaller. Two different numbers, two different impressions — and both are real.

**Key size facts:**
- A 1ct emerald cut is approximately **6.5mm × 4.5mm**
- A 2ct emerald cut is approximately **8.5mm × 6.0mm**
- A 3ct emerald cut is approximately **9.5mm × 7.0mm**
- A 4ct emerald cut is approximately **10.5mm × 7.8mm**
- A 5ct emerald cut is approximately **11.5mm × 8.5mm**

**The 3 factors that control visible size:**
1. Carat weight (heavier = larger, but not linearly)
2. Depth percentage (higher depth = smaller face-up size per carat)
3. Length-to-width ratio (longer L:W = more elongated, less width)

**The main comparison:** A 1ct emerald cut and a 1ct round brilliant both measure about 6.5mm in their longest dimension. The round measures 6.5mm in all directions. The emerald cut measures 6.5mm long but only 4.5mm wide. Longer. Narrower. Different.

→ **[Browse emerald cut diamonds by carat weight](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational)**

