## What Is an Emerald Cut Diamond Size Comparison?

An emerald cut diamond size comparison measures actual face-up dimensions — length and width in millimeters — against carat weight. The carat is a unit of mass, not size. Two emerald cuts of the same carat weight can show different face-up dimensions depending on how the cutter proportioned the depth.

I'm **Farzana Hasan**, a GIA-certified gemologist. I've [reviewed emerald cut diamonds](/emerald-cut-diamond) across every carat weight and every proportion. The size question is the one buyers ask most.

The answer always requires three numbers — carat weight, face-up dimensions, and depth percentage — because none of them tells the full story alone.

Full credentials and methodology at **[Diamond Critics](https://diamondcritics.com/about-farzana/)**.

This chart covers every major size from 0.25ct to 6ct. It also addresses the three named concepts that explain why emerald cut size works differently than buyers expect: The Face-Up Illusion, The Depth Penalty, and The L:W Rule.

