## How Big Is a 1 Carat Emerald Cut Diamond?

A [1 carat emerald cut diamond](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is approximately **6.5mm × 4.5mm** face-up with a depth around 3.5mm. That's the standard for a well-cut stone at 1.35:1 L:W ratio and 62% depth.

On a size 6 finger, a 1ct emerald cut covers about half the finger width in its width dimension (4.5mm against a typical 16mm finger width). In the length dimension (6.5mm), it's more than half the finger width. The stone is visible and clearly present without being oversized.

The 1ct emerald cut is the most [popular entry point](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for this shape. Full buying details including price ranges and setting recommendations are in the [1 carat emerald cut diamond ring guide](/1-carat-emerald-cut-diamond-ring).

---

## How Big Is a 1.5 Carat Emerald Cut Diamond?

A [1.5 carat emerald cut diamond](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=1.4&caratMax=1.6&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is approximately **7.5mm × 5.5mm** face-up with a depth around 4.0mm.

The jump from 1ct (6.5 × 4.5mm) to 1.5ct (7.5 × 5.5mm) is the most noticeable size increase per dollar in the emerald cut range. The 1ct to 1.5ct step adds 1mm in both length and width — a meaningful visual jump. On a size 6 finger, the 1.5ct emerald cut fills the finger noticeably more than the 1ct.

The 1.5ct emerald cut is the sweet spot for buyers who want clear presence without the sharp price jump to 2ct. [Browse 1.5ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=1.4&caratMax=1.6&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for current certified inventory.

