## How Big Is a 3 Carat Emerald Cut Diamond?

A [3 carat emerald cut diamond](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=2.9&caratMax=3.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) is approximately **9.5mm × 7.0mm** face-up with a depth around 5.1mm. This is the threshold where most people call it a large diamond.

On a size 6 finger, a 3ct emerald cut at 9.5mm length covers more than half the finger width. The stone is clearly visible from any angle. The hall-of-mirrors step-cut reflection pattern at this size creates long, sweeping flashes of light across a nearly 1cm face.

What does a 3 carat emerald cut diamond look like? The step-cut facets at 9.5mm × 7.0mm create the full hall-of-mirrors effect at a scale where it becomes dramatic rather than subtle. You see long rectangular reflections sweeping across nearly a centimeter of polished surface.

Full 3ct guide at [3 carat emerald cut diamond ring](/3-carat-emerald-cut-diamond-ring).

**How many mm is a 3 carat emerald cut diamond?** Approximately 9.5mm × 7.0mm for a well-cut stone. The range across real stones is approximately 9.0–10.0mm × 6.8–7.4mm depending on L:W ratio and depth percentage.

