**Important note on this table:** These estimates assume standard 1.30–1.40:1 L:W ratios and 60–65% depth. A stone with unusual proportions — particularly high depth (67%+) or very different L:W ratio — will deviate significantly. The only accurate way to determine carat weight is to weigh the stone on a calibrated scale or read the GIA/IGI grading report.

