## FAQs

### How big is a 1 carat emerald cut diamond?

A 1 carat emerald cut diamond is approximately **6.5mm × 4.5mm** face-up, with a depth of about 3.5mm. The exact dimensions depend on how the stone is cut — a shallower cut (60% depth) runs slightly larger, and a deeper cut (65%+) runs slightly smaller. [Browse 1ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=0.9&caratMax=1.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and check the listed dimensions — most certifications list L×W×D in millimeters.

### How big is a 2 carat emerald cut diamond?

A 2 carat emerald cut diamond is approximately **8.5mm × 6.0mm** face-up. That's about 1.3cm in its longest dimension. On a size 6 finger, the 2ct emerald cut is a clearly visible, statement-sized stone.

[Browse 2ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=1.9&caratMax=2.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and check the listed L×W for each stone — avoid any stone with dimensions significantly smaller than 8.2mm × 5.8mm at 2 carats, as that indicates excess depth.

### How big is a 3 carat emerald cut diamond?

A 3 carat emerald cut diamond is approximately **9.5mm × 7.0mm** face-up — just under 1cm in length. At this size, the hall-of-mirrors step-cut reflection pattern becomes dramatic: broad, slow sweeps of light across nearly a centimeter of polished table. [Browse 3ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=2.9&caratMax=3.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

Target 9.0mm × 6.8mm minimum at 3 carats to avoid The Depth Penalty.

### How many mm is a 2 carat emerald cut diamond?

A 2 carat emerald cut diamond is approximately **8.5mm long and 6.0mm wide**. These are typical dimensions for a well-cut stone at 1.35:1 L:W ratio and 62–63% depth. The listed dimensions on the GIA or IGI report are the authoritative measurement.

Search listings by L×W using the [emerald cut diamond search](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=1.9&caratMax=2.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) — filter to minimum 8.0mm length for best face-up size at 2ct.

### What carat is a 3×2mm emerald cut diamond?

A 3×2mm emerald cut diamond is approximately **0.07–0.10 carats** — a very small melee-grade stone. At 3mm long and 2mm wide, this is typically used as a channel-set accent stone, not a center stone. The 3×2mm emerald cut is rarely sold individually and is more commonly priced by the lot or by weight for accent stone applications.

### How many carats is an emerald cut diamond 3mm × 4mm?

A 4×3mm emerald cut diamond (4mm length, 3mm width) is approximately **0.20–0.27 carats**. At a 1.33:1 L:W ratio and standard depth, this is a small accent or solitaire stone. The carat weight is highly variable based on depth — a 4×3mm stone at 60% depth weighs less than the same surface dimensions at 65% depth.

### What carat is a 10×8mm emerald cut diamond?

A 10×8mm emerald cut diamond is approximately **3.5–4.5 carats**, depending heavily on depth percentage. The 10×8mm dimensions represent a wider L:W ratio (1.25:1) than the typical 1.35:1, so the stone sits squarer than standard. At standard 63–64% depth, a 10×8mm emerald cut weighs approximately 3.8–4.2 carats.

[Browse emerald cuts in this range](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=3.5&caratMax=4.5&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) and check listed dimensions.

### How many mm is a 6 carat emerald cut diamond?

A 6 carat emerald cut diamond is approximately **12.5mm × 9.0mm** face-up. This is 1.25cm in length — visibly large from any distance. The 6ct emerald cut is uncommon in natural stones due to cost and availability, but available in lab-grown format.

[Browse 6ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=5.8&caratMax=6.2&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for current inventory.

### Do emerald cut diamonds look bigger than round?

Emerald cuts look longer than rounds of the same carat weight, but not bigger in every direction. A 1ct emerald cut and a 1ct round are both approximately 6.5mm in their longest dimension. The round is 6.5mm in all directions; the emerald cut is only 4.5mm in the perpendicular direction.

The emerald cut looks elongated and impressive from above; the round looks larger from the sides and in total area coverage.

### Do emerald cut diamonds look smaller than they are?

Emerald cut diamonds can look smaller than a round of the same carat weight when compared by width. The emerald cut is always narrower than a round of the same carat because the rectangular shape concentrates the length. They can also look smaller than their carat weight suggests when cut with excessive depth — see The Depth Penalty section above.

A well-cut emerald cut at 60–63% depth looks appropriately sized for its carat weight.

### What is a good depth percentage for an emerald cut diamond?

Target **60–64% total depth** for an emerald cut diamond. Below 58% and the stone may look glassy and shallow — the step-cut facets lose their reflection depth. Above 65% and The Depth Penalty becomes significant — you're paying for carat weight hidden in the pavilion.

The depth percentage is listed on every GIA and IGI grading report and in the stone listing details on certified diamond retailers.

### How does L:W ratio affect emerald cut size on the finger?

L:W ratio directly changes how the stone fills your finger. A 1.50:1 L:W ratio creates a longer, slimmer stone that visually elongates the finger. A 1.25:1 L:W ratio creates a shorter, wider stone that fills the finger more evenly.

At the same carat weight, a higher L:W stone is longer and narrower; a lower L:W stone is shorter and wider. Neither is inherently "bigger" — the total face-up area is similar, but the shape impression is very different.

### How big is a 1.5 carat emerald cut diamond?

A 1.5 carat emerald cut diamond is approximately **7.5mm × 5.5mm** face-up. The jump from 1ct to 1.5ct adds about 1mm in each direction — a clearly visible increase. The 1.5ct is the most efficient size jump in the emerald cut range: you gain real face-up area without doubling the budget.

[Browse 1.5ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=1.4&caratMax=1.6&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational) for current availability.

### How big is a 4 carat emerald cut diamond?

A 4 carat emerald cut diamond is approximately **10.5mm × 7.8mm** face-up — just over 1cm in length. At this size, the stone visually covers most of the space between the knuckle joint and the finger base when viewed from above. The step-cut facets at 10.5mm create very long, slow reflections.

[Browse 4ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=3.9&caratMax=4.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

### How big is a 5 carat emerald cut diamond?

A 5 carat emerald cut diamond is approximately **11.5mm × 8.5mm** face-up. In both natural and lab-grown formats, the 5ct emerald cut is a large statement stone. The 11.5mm length is nearly the width of a US dime (17.9mm diameter).

[Browse 5ct emerald cuts](https://www.bluenile.com/diamond-search?shape=emerald&caratMin=4.9&caratMax=5.1&a_aid=69d7c31a91b8d&a_cid=55e51e63&chan=blog-informational).

### What is the typical length-to-width ratio for an emerald cut?

The typical L:W ratio for an emerald cut diamond is **1.30:1 to 1.50:1**, with 1.35:1 being the most common. Below 1.25:1 the stone looks too square; above 1.60:1 the stone looks stretched. The emerald cut name can technically apply to any rectangular step-cut, so always check the listed L:W ratio in addition to the carat weight.

See the [elongated emerald cut diamond guide](/elongated-emerald-cut-diamond) for higher L:W ratios (1.50:1 and above).

